<title>LEBANON: Lebanon public debt seen up 30 pct Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>Lebanon public debt seen up 30 pct Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's public debt rose by nearly 30 percent in the first 10 months of the year, according to figures issued by the Lebanese Banks Association (billions of Lebanese pounds at end of period unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>			 Dec 95   Aug 96   Sep 96   Oct 96 Dec95-Oct96</p>
<p>									  %</p>
<p>Revenues (Cumulative)3,033  2,169    2,461    2,748</p>
<p>Monthly change		    326	292	287</p>
<p>Expenses (Cumulative)5,739  4,159    4,937    5,998</p>
<p>Monthly change		    613	778    1,061</p>
<p>Deficit (Cumulative) 2,706  1,990    2,476    3,250</p>
<p>Monthly change		    287	486	774</p>
<p>Ratio deficit</p>
<p>to expenses	    0.47     0.48     0.50     0.54</p>
<p>Total debt	   14,079   16,770   17,755   18,244  29.58</p>
<p>Month change(%)	1.92     5.87     2.75</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 353078 645456</p>
